  LADDER.md.  Track L touched only `deltanet_decode_fx`'s q/k slicing
  and key-head index inside this file (both no-ops at LNKH == LNH) and
  added `_require_pow2_n`; neither is on the attention path and neither
  consumes RNG, so the expectation is PRE-EXISTING.  The baseline run is
  what decides it, not that expectation.

Nothing else at 0.8B/2B moved.  Every change is behind `VREP > 1`,
`n_shards > 1` or `not tied` — all false there — or is a new table
entry (the `w4g128gptq` quant).  Two independent confirmations in this
log: `load_qwen35.py`'s 2B smoke reproduces the committed raw-byte
